    {
      "id": "sol.amc-8-1991-p10.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Side \\(BC\\) runs from \\((0,2)\\) to \\((4,2),\\) so the base is \\(4.\\) The opposite side \\(AD\\) lies on the \\(x\\)-axis, so the height is \\(2.\\)\n\nThe area is \\(4 \\times 2 = 8.\\)\n\nThus, the correct answer is B .",
      "hints": [
        "Take \\(\\overline{BC}\\) as the base; it is horizontal from \\(B(0,2)\\) to \\(C(4,2)\\)",
        "The area is base times height, where the height is the vertical distance between the two horizontal sides"
      ],
